{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' <TMPDIR>/plan.txt\"","aggregated_output":"## Approach\n\nImplement Fix A + Fix B only. Fix C (Step 3 stdout keepalive heartbeat) is dropped per plan review (six reviewers, `[SCOPE-REDUCTION]`): Fix A alone breaks the deadlock, and a stdout heartbeat risks prefixing the completion output so the existing first-200-char \"prefix-identical repeat -> silent-yield\" rule hides the true completion notification. Fix C (heartbeat / premature-notification prevention) and Fix D (upstream Claude Code report) are out of scope here; capture them as follow-ups.\n\nRoot fix (Fix A): once the hook lets the orchestrator `Read` the write-once task-output file during a live wait, it can confirm the output is empty and apply the existing silent-yield rule instead of looping on denied probes. Fix B makes every loaded contract surface say so, so the orchestrator actually takes that path.\n\n1. Fix A -- allow `Read` of `tasks/*.output` during a live same-clone bg wait.\n   - In `scripts/hook-bg-poll-guard.sh`, in the `Read` branch (~line 1150), remove ONLY the `path_is_task_output \"$read_path\" && bash_probe_target_dir_plausible \"$dir\" \"$cwd_canon\"` OR-arm. Keep the `path_under_dir` and `path_is_known_result` arms unchanged: task outputs never satisfy them, so removing just this arm fully un-gates task-output reads without weakening marker-dir, result-env, or sentinel guards.\n   - Delete the now-orphaned `path_is_task_output` helper (defined ~line 695, used only at the removed arm) and rewrite the stale `#5925` comment block (~lines 1142-1149) that explains the old denial.\n   - Leave the Bash-command probe path denied: `cat`/`wc`/`stat` of `tasks/*.output` stays a polling probe and stays denied (the separate Bash arm ~lines 1046-1052 and `bash_probe_target_dir_plausible` are untouched).\n   - Keep every other guard intact: `TaskOutput`/`Monitor` denials, same-clone marker-dir reads, result-env reads, and terminal-sentinel polling.\n\n2. Fix B -- document one post-notification `Read` for emptiness classification across all loaded contract surfaces (no heartbeat wording, since Fix C is dropped).\n   - Contract: after a `<task-notification>` the orchestrator MAY perform exactly one `Read` of the active `tasks/*.output` to classify empty vs non-empty. Empty/missing -> silent-yield. Non-empty -> the existing single terminal-sentinel probe, then routing. This is not progress polling and is distinct from the after-completion result parse.\n\n## Files to modify/create\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/hook-bg-poll-guard.sh\n\n- Remove the `tasks/*.output` `Read` deny arm at ~line 1150; keep the `path_under_dir` and `path_is_known_result` arms.\n- Delete the orphaned `path_is_task_output` helper; rewrite the stale `#5925` comment block.\n- Leave Bash-probe task-output matching and `bash_probe_target_dir_plausible` clone-gating unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/hook-bg-poll-guard.md\n\n- Update invariants: `Read` of `tasks/*.output` is allowed during live waits (write-once completion artifact); Bash probes of it and the `TaskOutput` tool remain denied; the carve-out exists so the orchestrator can classify empty spurious output after a premature notification.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/test-hook-bg-poll-guard.sh\n\n- Flip the `live marker + Read tasks/foo.output` assertions from deny to allow, running them from a repo-clone cwd DISTINCT from the marker dir (per accepted FINDING_3).\n- Add or keep a separate assertion that a `Read` of a path UNDER the live marker dir 
